  "description": "Reid Bikes H16 | 16 inch kids' bike\nBig on fun, light on weight – the ultimate 16\" kids' first pedal bike for 3-6 year olds, to help build skills and confidence.\nWeighing in at just 5.4kg, this Reid Bikes 16\" kids' bike offers an unbeatable combination of lightweight performance and durability at an incredible price. Easier to ride, easier to carry, and easier to love – it's the perfect step up for young riders ready to take things further.\nPart of the Reid Bikes H Series kids' bike range, this H16 kids' bike is crafted from lightweight 6061 alloy for both frame and fork, the bike delivers excellent strength without the bulk. The simple single-speed setup with a 25T chainring and 15T freewheel keeps riding intuitive, letting kids focus on balance, steering, and fun.\nKid-optimised components like short-reach alloy brake levers, a 100mm alloy crank, and a comfy junior saddle ensure a secure and confident fit. Reliable Jak V-brakes, and the 16 x 1.5\" Vee tires provide all-surface grip for rides around the park, driveway, or schoolyard. From first real adventures to everyday rides, this ultra-light bike gives young riders the best possible start – more control, more comfort, and more reasons to keep riding.\nWho is the Reid Bikes H16 for?\nThe H16 kids' bike is ideal for:\n\n3–6 year olds ready for their next step on two wheels\n\nYoung riders developing their cycling skills, including balance, steering and braking\n\nChildren moving up from a balance bike or smaller kids' bike and ready to ride further\n\nYoung adventurers who want more freedom and independence on two wheels\n\nEveryday rides and family adventures, from the park and schoolyard to local bike paths\n\nParents looking for a lightweight, easy-to-control bike that makes riding more enjoyable for young cyclists\n\nFind the right fit\nChoosing the right bike size helps your child ride comfortably, confidently and safely. Use our Kids' Bike Size Guide by clicking the tab above to find the right Reid bike based on your child’s height and age.",
